@startuml Agent Life v2 - API Sequence Diagrams
!theme vibrant
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam shadowing true

title Agent Life v2 - Key API Interaction Sequences

== Scenario 1: Create and Start Cycle ==

actor User #4169E1
participant "Frontend" as FE #32CD32
participant "API\n(Flask)" as API #FF8C00
participant "Cycle\nManager" as CM #FF69B4
participant "Constellation\nManager" as ConstM #9370DB
participant "Database" as DB #FFD700
participant "Action\nOrchestrator" as AO #00CED1

User -> FE : Fill cycle form
activate FE

FE -> FE : Validate inputs\nclient-side

FE -> API : POST /api/agentlife/cycles/\n{name, days, agents, ...}
activate API

API -> API : Authenticate\nuser (JWT)

API -> CM : create_cycle(user_id, data)
activate CM

CM -> ConstM : validate_constellation_id()
activate ConstM
ConstM -> DB : SELECT constellation
activate DB
DB --> ConstM : constellation data
deactivate DB
ConstM --> CM : valid
deactivate ConstM

CM -> CM : Validate:\n• Days (1-30)\n• Agents exist\n• Required fields

CM -> DB : INSERT cycle_configurations
activate DB
DB --> CM : cycle object
deactivate DB

CM --> API : cycle created
deactivate CM

API --> FE : 201 Created\n{cycle: {...}}
deactivate API

FE -> FE : Update Pinia store
FE --> User : Show success message\nDisplay cycle in list
deactivate FE

|||

User -> FE : Click "Start"
activate FE

FE -> API : POST /api/agentlife/cycles/<id>/start/
activate API

API -> CM : start_cycle(cycle_id, user_id)
activate CM

CM -> DB : INSERT cycle_executions\nstatus='queued'
activate DB
DB --> CM : execution object
deactivate DB

CM -> AO : queue_execution(execution_id)
activate AO
AO -> AO : Create background\ntask/thread
AO --> CM : queued
deactivate AO

CM --> API : execution started
deactivate CM

API --> FE : 200 OK\n{execution: {...}}
deactivate API

FE -> FE : Navigate to\nMonitor tab
FE -> FE : Subscribe to\nSocket.IO events
FE --> User : Show monitoring\ndashboard
deactivate FE

== Scenario 2: Pause and Resume Cycle ==

User -> FE : Click "Pause"
activate FE

FE -> FE : Confirm dialog

FE -> API : POST /api/agentlife/cycles/\nexecutions/<id>/pause/
activate API

API -> CM : pause_execution(execution_id, user_id)
activate CM

CM -> DB : SELECT execution
activate DB
DB --> CM : execution data
deactivate DB

CM -> CM : Check status\n(must be 'running')

CM -> DB : UPDATE status='paused'\npaused_at=NOW()
activate DB
DB --> CM : updated
deactivate DB

CM -> AO : pause_execution_signal(execution_id)
activate AO
AO -> AO : Set pause flag\nwait for current action
AO --> CM : pausing
deactivate AO

CM -> CM : Broadcast Socket.IO:\ncycle_status_update

CM --> API : execution paused
deactivate CM

API --> FE : 200 OK\n{execution: {status: 'paused'}}
deactivate API

FE -> FE : Update UI:\n• Disable pause button\n• Enable resume button
FE --> User : Visual confirmation
deactivate FE

|||

User -> FE : Click "Resume"
activate FE

FE -> API : POST /api/agentlife/cycles/\nexecutions/<id>/resume/
activate API

API -> CM : resume_execution(execution_id, user_id)
activate CM

CM -> DB : UPDATE status='running'
activate DB
DB --> CM : updated
deactivate DB

CM -> AO : resume_execution_signal(execution_id)
activate AO
AO -> AO : Clear pause flag\ncontinue from next action
AO --> CM : resuming
deactivate AO

CM -> CM : Broadcast Socket.IO:\ncycle_status_update

CM --> API : execution resumed
deactivate CM

API --> FE : 200 OK\n{execution: {status: 'running'}}
deactivate API

FE -> FE : Update UI:\n• Enable pause button\n• Disable resume button
FE --> User : Execution continues
deactivate FE

== Scenario 3: Real-Time Monitoring ==

participant "Socket.IO\nClient" as Socket #FF6347
participant "Socket.IO\nServer" as SocketSrv #DC143C
participant "Status\nAggregator" as SA #FF1493

FE -> Socket : Subscribe to\nexecution updates
activate Socket
activate FE

Socket -> SocketSrv : emit('subscribe_cycle_updates',\n{execution_id, user_id})
activate SocketSrv

SocketSrv -> SocketSrv : Join room\n'cycle_<execution_id>'

SocketSrv --> Socket : Subscribed
SocketSrv --> FE : Ready
deactivate Socket

note over FE, AO
  Background: Cycle executing
end note

AO -> SA : Notify action started
activate SA
activate AO

SA -> DB : INSERT log
activate DB
DB --> SA : logged
deactivate DB

SA -> SocketSrv : emit('agent_action_started',\ndata)
SocketSrv --> FE : Broadcast event
deactivate SA

FE -> FE : Update Pinia store:\n• agentStatuses[agent_id]\n• Add to logs array

FE -> FE : Update UI:\n• Agent card badge\n• Progress bar\n• Log viewer
FE --> User : Real-time update
deactivate AO

|||

AO -> SA : Notify action completed
activate SA
activate AO

SA -> DB : INSERT log
activate DB
DB --> SA : logged
deactivate DB

SA -> DB : UPDATE execution\ncompleted_actions++
activate DB
DB --> SA : updated
deactivate DB

SA -> SocketSrv : emit('agent_action_completed',\ndata)
SocketSrv --> FE : Broadcast event
deactivate SA

FE -> FE : Update store & UI
FE --> User : Show completion
deactivate AO
deactivate FE
deactivate SocketSrv

== Scenario 4: Fetch Execution Logs ==

User -> FE : Scroll logs viewer\nto top
activate FE

FE -> FE : Check if need\nmore logs

FE -> API : GET /api/agentlife/cycles/\nexecutions/<id>/logs/\n?limit=100&offset=100
activate API

API -> CM : get_execution_logs(execution_id, ...)
activate CM

CM -> DB : SELECT * FROM logs\nWHERE execution_id=...\nLIMIT 100 OFFSET 100
activate DB
DB --> CM : log entries
deactivate DB

CM --> API : logs array
deactivate CM

API --> FE : 200 OK\n{logs: [...], total: 500}
deactivate API

FE -> FE : Prepend logs\nto existing array

FE -> FE : Update log viewer\nscroll position
FE --> User : Display older logs
deactivate FE

legend right
  |= Component |= Color |
  | <back:#4169E1>   </back> | User |
  | <back:#32CD32>   </back> | Frontend |
  | <back:#FF8C00>   </back> | API |
  | <back:#FF69B4>   </back> | CycleManager |
  | <back:#9370DB>   </back> | ConstellationManager |
  | <back:#FFD700>   </back> | Database |
  | <back:#00CED1>   </back> | ActionOrchestrator |
  | <back:#FF6347>   </back> | Socket.IO Client |
  | <back:#DC143C>   </back> | Socket.IO Server |
  | <back:#FF1493>   </back> | StatusAggregator |
endlegend

@enduml
